1. **Open Xcode**: Launch Xcode and create a new project. Choose "App" as the template and select "SwiftUI App" for the language.

2. **Define Your View**: In the main file, typically `ContentView.swift`, you can define your UI. Here’s a basic example:

```swift
import SwiftUI

struct ContentView: View {
    var body: some View {
        VStack {
            Text("Hello, SwiftUI!")
                .font(.largeTitle)
                .padding()
            Button(action: {
                print("Button pressed!")
            }) {
                Text("Press Me")
                    .font(.title)
                    .padding()
            }
        }
        .padding()
    }
}

@main
struct MyApp: App {
    var body: some Scene {
        WindowGroup {
            ContentView()
        }
    }
}
```

